      "solution": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    // Read the number of customers\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n\n    // Array to store the frequency of each time (0 to 100)\n    int counts[101] = {0}; \n    int t;\n\n    // Read inputs and tally them up in a single pass\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        scanf(\"%d\", &t);\n        counts[t]++;\n    }\n\n    long long total_wait_time = 0;\n    long long current_running_time = 0;\n\n    // Iterate through our frequency array\n    for (int i = 1; i <= 100; i++) {\n        // If we have customers with this wait time, process them\n        while (counts[i] > 0) {\n            current_running_time += i;\n            total_wait_time += current_running_time;\n            counts[i]--;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Print the result (using %lld because we used long long)\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", total_wait_time);\n\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "statement": "You are a solo barista at a coffee shop, and suddenly [[N]] customers walk in at the exact same time. Each customer orders a drink that takes a specific amount of time [[T]] to prepare.\n\nA customer's \"wait time\" is the sum of the preparation times of everyone served before them, plus the time it takes to make their own drink.\n\nTo prevent a riot, you decide to make the drinks in an order that minimizes the total combined wait time of all customers. Find that minimum total wait time.",
